flowchart TB
  accTitle: Local-First Meeting Transcription architecture
  accDescr: A React UI streams microphone or shared-tab audio to a local FastAPI backend. Vosk writes a live transcript during the meeting and faster-whisper writes a refined one from the saved audio afterward. A review queue reconciles the two, and a person verifies or edits the result. Audio, transcripts, and exports stay in local SQLite and on disk. Only the agreed transcript is sent to the configured Ollama-compatible notes model, which returns structured notes.

  subgraph browser["BROWSER · REACT"]
    ui["`**Meeting UI**
    live, review, export`"]
  end

  subgraph machine["THIS MACHINE · FASTAPI"]
    capture["`**Capture**
    mic or shared tab`"]
    live["`**Live pass**
    Vosk, during`"]
    refined["`**Refined pass**
    faster-whisper, after`"]
    review["`**Review queue**
    reconcile both`"]
    store[("`**SQLite + disk**
    audio, transcripts`")]
  end

  notes["`**Notes model**
  Ollama-compatible endpoint,
  returns structured notes`"]

  ui ==>|audio| capture
  capture ==> live
  capture --> store
  store --> refined
  live ==> review
  refined ==> review
  ui -->|verify, edit| review
  review ==>|agreed transcript| notes

  classDef key fill:#e6eee9,stroke:#315e55,stroke-width:2.5px,color:#192c32
  classDef ext fill:#f7f8f5,stroke:#7c8f83,color:#192c32
  classDef side fill:#f7f8f5,stroke:#b6c3ba,stroke-dasharray:6 4,color:#526460
  class review key
  class notes ext
